      "writtenOn": "2020-04-07T17:13:45Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "No this is not to prevent internal merge conflict. That tag has been put there because we have detected vendors using/overriding/extending this class in their implementations of this code.\n\nThat tag unofficially adds the class to a whitelist of accessible classes - if a new replacement is added, ART may block access to that class at runtime (depending on how it is accessed). To keep compatibility, if it is removed, the compilation will generate errors because the whitelist has changed to remove this unofficial API. So, we must keep this old class in for compatibility.",
